 "notes": "Strip b: x 2220-3530 plus ~300 px overlap (1920-3830). N-S streets: Vaughn Street (~1968), Eden Avenue (~2307-2330, leans slightly east going south), Gerard Street (~2657-2683), Bellevue Avenue (~3008-3032), Highland Avenue (~3620-3636, double track lines in it). Gerard printed 'STREET' near Goodman and 'GERARD' further south; Bellevue and Highland printed 'AVENUE' in the north part, names further south: assumed continuous. Vaughn printed 'VAUGHN' south of University, only 'ST.' between St. Clair and Rochelle (assumed Vaughn). Melish printed 'MELISH' with no suffix seen (recorded Melish Avenue); Oak printed 'OAK' with no suffix seen (recorded Oak Street); E. Auburn suffix not seen (recorded East Auburn Avenue); E. McMillan suffix not seen (recorded East McMillan Street). East of Eden the street at y~5955 is printed only 'ST.' and taken as the jogged continuation of E. Corry. West of Eden: French, E. Nixon, Goodman, an unnamed 50 ft street at y~2040, E. St. Clair, E. Rochelle, E. University, E. Daniels, E. Charlton, E. Corry, E. Auburn. East of Eden: Piedmont, Melish, Stetson, Rochelle, Donahue, University, Fosdick, Oak, Corry ('ST.'), Auburn. Hospital (Cincinnati General) fills the block Bethesda/Eden/Goodman/diagonal; its DRIVEs are not streets. 'ERKENBRECHER', 'W.M. CORRY', 'DONAHUE' etc. printed diagonally across blocks are subdivision/owner labels. Narrow unnamed alley at x~1976 between Charlton and Corry recorded in alleys. Burnet Avenue (x~4235) and the Ridgeway junction lie outside this strip."
